As chassisArray is an array, I think "Chassis@odata.count" seem needed.
Please also verify it with Redfish Service Validator.

```
 asyncResp->res.jsonValue["Links"]["Chassis@odata.count"] = chassisArray.size();
 asyncResp->res.jsonValue["Links"]["Chassis"] = std::move(chassisArray);
```

I think combination of `getValidSystemsPath()` and `getAssociatedSubTreePaths()` can be done by `getAssociatedSubTreePathsById()` something like

```
    constexpr std::array<std::string_view, 2> systemInterfaces = {
        "xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.ManagedHost",
        "xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.System"};

    dbus::utility::getAssociatedSubTreePathsById(
        systemName, "/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory", systemInterfaces,
        "contained_by", chassisInterfaces,
        std::bind_front(getLinkedChassis, asyncResp, systemName));
```

